B.air=new A.j0("Pride and Prejudice: plates by Hugh Thomson (George Allen, 1894) and C. E. Brock (Macmillan, 1895). Frankenstein: frontispiece and title-page vignette by Theodor von Holst, engraved by W. Chevalier (Colburn & Bentley, 1831). All are public domain; scans from Wikimedia Commons. Full per-plate sources are listed in the app\u2019s attribution file.",null)
B.ais=new A.j0("Definitions come from Webster\u2019s Revised Unabridged Dictionary (G. & C. Merriam Co., 1913), a public-domain work, via the Project Gutenberg text (gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765) as parsed by the WebstersEnglishDictionary project on GitHub. Definitions are shortened to their first senses; being from 1913, they reflect the usage and attitudes of their time.",null)
B.ait=new A.j0("All books come from Standard Ebooks (standardebooks.org), a volunteer project that produces carefully proofread, beautifully formatted editions of public-domain works.",null)
B.aiu=new A.j0("Recordings are LibriVox (librivox.org) public-domain audiobooks read by volunteers, streamed from the Internet Archive (archive.org); each player names its reader. Read-along timing for a few pilot chapters was produced on our side by automatically aligning the recording with the text, so it can drift by a word or two. Liber et Libri is not affiliated with LibriVox or the Internet Archive.",null)
B.aiv=new A.j0("For reading in the app, the text has been converted to plain paragraphs; endnotes and some typographic details were left out.",null)
